
"smart_sources:Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/culture/Culture - Naval Officers.md": {"path":"Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/culture/Culture - Naval Officers.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"1rjz26x","at":1777331817895},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1777002481301,"size":1902,"at":1777331817921,"hash":"1rjz26x"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,17],"#Culture - Naval Officers":[19,20],"#A rising social and economic class in Flora, comprised of successful naval officers.":[21,25],"#A rising social and economic class in Flora, comprised of successful naval officers.#{1}":[22,25]},"outlinks":[],"metadata":{"type":"lore","status":"active","priority":50,"tags":["#lorebook"],"keys":["naval officer","nouveau riche","new money","admiralty"],"position":"before","depth":4,"scanDepth":1,"summary":"**What this is:** A rising social/economic class in Flora consisting of successful naval officers who gain wealth primarily through prize money from captured enemy/pirate vessels.\n\n**When to select:** When focusing on Flora's social hierarchy, political tensions, characters from diverse backgrounds who have risen socially, or the rivalries between \"old money\" aristocracy and \"new money\" military elite. Relevant if discussing Eleanor Castor (the user's mother) as an example of this class.\n\n**Key relationships:** Opposed by the old aristocracy who resent their wealth and influence; includes officers from varied birth who purchase commissions; women have promotion advantages."},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/culture/Culture - Naval Officers.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"1vdrqua","at":1777331817895},"key":"Lore for Flora's Regency Era (UPDATED)/culture/Culture - Naval Officers.md#---frontmatter---","lines":[1,17],"size":893,"outlinks":[],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
